// The guide to one robot: facts about this robot that a caller needs to
// drive it well and that no other contract gives. The launcher that brings
// the robot up measures them and writes them for its model, so the facts
// belong to the robot: a caller that drives robots of many models, such as a
// chat agent, asks each robot and keeps no list of models.
//
// The guide holds the park pose of each arm that the launcher gives one
// for: a joint configuration that holds the arm up, above the surface it
// works on and out of the view of the perception camera (workspace defines
// it). An arm that starts a move down to the surface from its park pose
// comes from above, over what stands on the surface, and not through it. A
// caller parks an arm with move_arm_joints of limb_motion.
//
// Slicing rule for the arrays: park_joint_positions concatenates the joints
// of each arm of park_arm_names in that order; arm i's vector starts at the
// sum of park_joints_per_arm[0..i] and runs park_joints_per_arm[i] entries,
// in the arm's joint order of limb_motion.
//
// Joints are in radians (meters for a prismatic joint). Arm names are the
// names limb_motion addresses the arms by. An empty guide is a valid answer:
// the launcher gave no park pose for this robot.
{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "robot_guide",
    tag: "v1",
  },
  interfaces: {
    services: [
      {
        name: "get_guide",
        response_message_format: {
          // The arms that have a park pose, in the robot's arm order.
          park_arm_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string" },
          // Joint count of each arm, index-aligned with park_arm_names.
          park_joints_per_arm: { $type: "array", $items: "u32" },
          // The joints of each park pose, each arm's vector concatenated in
          // park_arm_names order.
          park_joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64" },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
}
